[{"text": "I now give the floor to his excellency", "start": 3.76, "duration": 8.56}, {"text": "Carlos Ramiro Martinez Alvarado,", "start": 7.44, "duration": 6.72}, {"text": "Minister of Foreign Affairs of", "start": 12.32, "duration": 4.84}, {"text": "Guatemala.", "start": 14.16, "duration": 3.0}, {"text": ">> Mr. the president of the General", "start": 28.0, "duration": 5.6}, {"text": "Assembly. Excellencies,", "start": 29.519, "duration": 6.241}, {"text": "ladies and gentlemen,", "start": 33.6, "duration": 4.4}, {"text": "the international system that has guided", "start": 35.76, "duration": 4.959}, {"text": "our relations over recent decades is", "start": 38.0, "duration": 5.6}, {"text": "undergoing a profound transformation.", "start": 40.719, "duration": 6.081}, {"text": "Conflicts, geopolitical tensions,", "start": 43.6, "duration": 5.84}, {"text": "declining resources for development, and", "start": 46.8, "duration": 5.52}, {"text": "the fragmentation of spaces for dialogue", "start": 49.44, "duration": 4.56}, {"text": "are testing the principles that have", "start": 52.32, "duration": 4.48}, {"text": "guided coexistence among nations. At the", "start": 54.0, "duration": 5.6}, {"text": "same time, democracy faces a two-fold", "start": 56.8, "duration": 4.48}, {"text": "challenge.", "start": 59.6, "duration": 3.52}, {"text": "The resurgence of authoritarian", "start": 61.28, "duration": 3.68}, {"text": "tendencies that seek to undermine the", "start": 63.12, "duration": 4.48}, {"text": "will of the people and the spread of", "start": 64.96, "duration": 4.96}, {"text": "organized criminal networks that", "start": 67.6, "duration": 5.44}, {"text": "infiltrate institutions, corrupt justice", "start": 69.92, "duration": 5.199}, {"text": "systems, capture economies and", "start": 73.04, "duration": 6.56}, {"text": "territories, and erode public trust.", "start": 75.119, "duration": 7.121}, {"text": "Transnational organized crime is more", "start": 79.6, "duration": 4.879}, {"text": "than just a threat to public security.", "start": 82.24, "duration": 4.72}, {"text": "It is a direct threat to democracy, the", "start": 84.479, "duration": 5.521}, {"text": "rule of law, and the ability of our", "start": 86.96, "duration": 4.799}, {"text": "peoples to freely determine their", "start": 90.0, "duration": 4.32}, {"text": "future. Criminal networks do not", "start": 91.759, "duration": 5.281}, {"text": "recognize borders. They are linked", "start": 94.32, "duration": 4.96}, {"text": "through drug trafficking, trafficking in", "start": 97.04, "duration": 4.64}, {"text": "persons, illicit arms trafficking,", "start": 99.28, "duration": 6.08}, {"text": "smuggling, extortion, money laundering,", "start": 101.68, "duration": 6.32}, {"text": "environmental crime, and other illicit", "start": 105.36, "duration": 5.52}, {"text": "economies. They exploit institutional", "start": 108.0, "duration": 5.68}, {"text": "weaknesses, inequality, and a lack of", "start": 110.88, "duration": 5.279}, {"text": "opportunities. Wherever the state is", "start": 113.68, "duration": 5.2}, {"text": "weakened, these structures seek to", "start": 116.159, "duration": 6.081}, {"text": "replace it, intimidate it, or bend it to", "start": 118.88, "duration": 5.76}, {"text": "serve private interests.", "start": 122.24, "duration": 4.72}, {"text": "In the face of these realities, the", "start": 124.64, "duration": 4.0}, {"text": "fundamental principles that must guide", "start": 126.96, "duration": 3.68}, {"text": "our collective action have lost none of", "start": 128.64, "duration": 4.72}, {"text": "their relevance. preserving peace,", "start": 130.64, "duration": 5.36}, {"text": "combating hunger and poverty, ensuring", "start": 133.36, "duration": 4.56}, {"text": "equal rights and opportunities,", "start": 136.0, "duration": 4.48}, {"text": "strengthening justice, protecting our", "start": 137.92, "duration": 4.8}, {"text": "planet, and consolidating democratic", "start": 140.48, "duration": 4.56}, {"text": "institutions remain shared", "start": 142.72, "duration": 4.4}, {"text": "responsibilities.", "start": 145.04, "duration": 4.16}, {"text": "The sustainable development goals", "start": 147.12, "duration": 4.0}, {"text": "continue to provide an essential", "start": 149.2, "duration": 5.36}, {"text": "roadmap. It is precisely at moments such", "start": 151.12, "duration": 5.199}, {"text": "as this", "start": 154.56, "duration": 4.72}, {"text": "that international law, multilateralism,", "start": 156.319, "duration": 5.601}, {"text": "and democracy show their worth.", "start": 159.28, "duration": 5.2}, {"text": "Law provides us with common rules.", "start": 161.92, "duration": 5.2}, {"text": "Multilateralism enables us to turn", "start": 164.48, "duration": 4.72}, {"text": "shared problems into concerted", "start": 167.12, "duration": 5.52}, {"text": "solutions. And democracy ensures that", "start": 169.2, "duration": 5.92}, {"text": "power comes from the people and is", "start": 172.64, "duration": 5.36}, {"text": "exercised for their well-being.", "start": 175.12, "duration": 4.479}, {"text": "I address this assembly on behalf of", "start": 178.0, "duration": 4.159}, {"text": "Guatemala, a country that knows from its", "start": 179.599, "duration": 5.441}, {"text": "own experience the value of these tools.", "start": 182.159, "duration": 4.961}, {"text": "Our history has taught us that", "start": 185.04, "duration": 4.8}, {"text": "democracy, peace, and respect for the", "start": 187.12, "duration": 6.24}, {"text": "law are not permanent achievements. They", "start": 189.84, "duration": 5.52}, {"text": "are built collectively, and each", "start": 193.36, "duration": 4.879}, {"text": "generation must preserve them. A", "start": 195.36, "duration": 5.599}, {"text": "democracy rests on free elections,", "start": 198.239, "duration": 5.041}, {"text": "legitimate institutions, the separation", "start": 200.959, "duration": 5.441}, {"text": "of powers, freedom of expression, public", "start": 203.28, "duration": 5.679}, {"text": "participation, transparency, and", "start": 206.4, "duration": 4.8}, {"text": "accountability.", "start": 208.959, "duration": 4.56}, {"text": "But it also requires independent and", "start": 211.2, "duration": 4.8}, {"text": "effective institutions committed to the", "start": 213.519, "duration": 4.961}, {"text": "constitution, the law and the popular", "start": 216.0, "duration": 4.48}, {"text": "mandate.", "start": 218.48, "duration": 4.24}, {"text": "Public institutions must not serve", "start": 220.48, "duration": 5.2}, {"text": "criminal networks, private agendas,", "start": 222.72, "duration": 5.439}, {"text": "personal loyalties or political or", "start": 225.68, "duration": 4.479}, {"text": "economic interests that are at odds with", "start": 228.159, "duration": 4.481}, {"text": "the common good. They must serve the", "start": 230.159, "duration": 5.281}, {"text": "people, the constitutional order, and", "start": 232.64, "duration": 6.319}, {"text": "society's democratic interests. When an", "start": 235.44, "duration": 6.48}, {"text": "institution strays from that purpose, it", "start": 238.959, "duration": 5.36}, {"text": "does more than simply lose legitimacy,", "start": 241.92, "duration": 4.56}, {"text": "it weakens the democracy it is meant to", "start": 244.319, "duration": 4.801}, {"text": "protect. Democracy also earns its", "start": 246.48, "duration": 4.88}, {"text": "legitimacy in everyday life. When a", "start": 249.12, "duration": 5.119}, {"text": "family is protected from poverty, when a", "start": 251.36, "duration": 5.839}, {"text": "child learns in a decent school, when a", "start": 254.239, "duration": 5.68}, {"text": "woman lives free from violence, when a", "start": 257.199, "duration": 5.361}, {"text": "community is no longer isolated, and", "start": 259.919, "duration": 4.56}, {"text": "when a young person can envision a", "start": 262.56, "duration": 3.84}, {"text": "future without being forced to leave", "start": 264.479, "duration": 4.881}, {"text": "their country. That is why in Guatemala", "start": 266.4, "duration": 5.44}, {"text": "we are restoring the state's capacity to", "start": 269.36, "duration": 5.44}, {"text": "reach those who have been excluded from", "start": 271.84, "duration": 6.16}, {"text": "opportunities for far too long. The", "start": 274.8, "duration": 6.08}, {"text": "intersectional manua mano strategy", "start": 278.0, "duration": 5.12}, {"text": "brings together health, education,", "start": 280.88, "duration": 4.319}, {"text": "housing, nutrition and community", "start": 283.12, "duration": 4.24}, {"text": "development to address poverty at the", "start": 285.199, "duration": 4.801}, {"text": "local level. Following crop losses", "start": 287.36, "duration": 5.04}, {"text": "caused by climate related events, more", "start": 290.0, "duration": 5.52}, {"text": "than 450,000 families have received food", "start": 292.4, "duration": 6.0}, {"text": "assistance, while small-scale producers", "start": 295.52, "duration": 5.84}, {"text": "have gained access to seeds, tools,", "start": 298.4, "duration": 6.0}, {"text": "inputs, and insurance mechanisms.", "start": 301.36, "duration": 5.119}, {"text": "Public education is central to this", "start": 304.4, "duration": 3.6}, {"text": "effort.", "start": 306.479, "duration": 3.041}, {"text": "More than 1 million students have", "start": 308.0, "duration": 3.12}, {"text": "participated in initiatives to", "start": 309.52, "duration": 4.0}, {"text": "strengthen reading comprehension. We", "start": 311.12, "duration": 4.88}, {"text": "have expanded educational opportunities,", "start": 313.52, "duration": 4.64}, {"text": "promoted scholarships, strengthened", "start": 316.0, "duration": 4.24}, {"text": "instruction in national languages, and", "start": 318.16, "duration": 3.84}, {"text": "accelerated the digital transformation", "start": 320.24, "duration": 5.12}, {"text": "of the school system. In healthcare, we", "start": 322.0, "duration": 5.36}, {"text": "have expanded and refurbished", "start": 325.36, "duration": 4.0}, {"text": "facilities, strengthened regional", "start": 327.36, "duration": 4.8}, {"text": "services, and made progress in the", "start": 329.36, "duration": 4.88}, {"text": "comprehensive treatment of chronic", "start": 332.16, "duration": 5.039}, {"text": "diseases and cancer. Alongside the", "start": 334.24, "duration": 4.959}, {"text": "revival of road projects and public", "start": 337.199, "duration": 4.0}, {"text": "works in historically underserved", "start": 339.199, "duration": 4.801}, {"text": "communities, the National Digital", "start": 341.199, "duration": 5.361}, {"text": "Connectivity Plan now provides internet", "start": 344.0, "duration": 7.52}, {"text": "service to 383 public entities. We have", "start": 346.56, "duration": 7.84}, {"text": "also strengthened early warning systems", "start": 351.52, "duration": 5.76}, {"text": "for earthquakes, tsunamis, floods, and", "start": 354.4, "duration": 5.519}, {"text": "volcano hazards.", "start": 357.28, "duration": 4.639}, {"text": "Restoring the legitimate presence of the", "start": 359.919, "duration": 4.961}, {"text": "state also means providing security in", "start": 361.919, "duration": 5.28}, {"text": "accordance with the law, strengthening", "start": 364.88, "duration": 5.28}, {"text": "prevention, protecting communities, and", "start": 367.199, "duration": 5.28}, {"text": "pursuing criminal networks rather than", "start": 370.16, "duration": 5.039}, {"text": "only their visible manifestations. It", "start": 372.479, "duration": 4.481}, {"text": "means improving investigations,", "start": 375.199, "duration": 3.921}, {"text": "institutional coordination, and the", "start": 376.96, "duration": 4.48}, {"text": "tracing of the financial flows that", "start": 379.12, "duration": 5.199}, {"text": "sustain illicit economies.", "start": 381.44, "duration": 5.039}, {"text": "Guatemala maintains that the charter of", "start": 384.319, "duration": 4.801}, {"text": "the United Nations and international law", "start": 386.479, "duration": 4.72}, {"text": "must remain our common point of", "start": 389.12, "duration": 4.48}, {"text": "reference.", "start": 391.199, "duration": 3.921}, {"text": "The sovereignty and territorial", "start": 393.6, "duration": 4.4}, {"text": "integrity of states must be respected.", "start": 395.12, "duration": 4.96}, {"text": "Disputes must be settled by peaceful", "start": 398.0, "duration": 5.84}, {"text": "means. Human rights must be protected.", "start": 400.08, "duration": 5.76}, {"text": "International humanitarian law must be", "start": 403.84, "duration": 4.56}, {"text": "observed in all circumstances.", "start": 405.84, "duration": 4.96}, {"text": "And international obligations must be", "start": 408.4, "duration": 4.48}, {"text": "fulfilled.", "start": 410.8, "duration": 4.56}, {"text": "The law loses its ability to protect us", "start": 412.88, "duration": 4.56}, {"text": "when we accept its selective", "start": 415.36, "duration": 3.92}, {"text": "application.", "start": 417.44, "duration": 4.0}, {"text": "National and international institutions", "start": 419.28, "duration": 4.8}, {"text": "lose legitimacy when they depart from", "start": 421.44, "duration": 5.199}, {"text": "their mandates in response to pressure,", "start": 424.08, "duration": 5.519}, {"text": "calculations or particular interests.", "start": 426.639, "duration": 6.081}, {"text": "Their authority rests on independence,", "start": 429.599, "duration": 5.681}, {"text": "impartiality, transparency and respect", "start": 432.72, "duration": 4.96}, {"text": "for the law. There can be no there", "start": 435.28, "duration": 4.24}, {"text": "cannot be one rule for the powerful and", "start": 437.68, "duration": 4.079}, {"text": "another for the weak. Nor can there be", "start": 439.52, "duration": 4.88}, {"text": "victims whose suffering outrages us and", "start": 441.759, "duration": 4.72}, {"text": "others whose suffering we choose to", "start": 444.4, "duration": 3.68}, {"text": "ignore.", "start": 446.479, "duration": 3.521}, {"text": "For countries such as Guatemala,", "start": 448.08, "duration": 4.32}, {"text": "international law does not constrain our", "start": 450.0, "duration": 5.36}, {"text": "sovereignty. It is one of its principal", "start": 452.4, "duration": 5.68}, {"text": "safeguards. Guatemala believes in the", "start": 455.36, "duration": 5.04}, {"text": "peaceful settlement of disputes. We", "start": 458.08, "duration": 3.92}, {"text": "place our trust in dialogue,", "start": 460.4, "duration": 4.239}, {"text": "negotiation, and the mechanisms provided", "start": 462.0, "duration": 5.759}, {"text": "for under international law because even", "start": 464.639, "duration": 5.84}, {"text": "the most complex historical differences", "start": 467.759, "duration": 5.361}, {"text": "can and must be resolved by peaceful", "start": 470.479, "duration": 4.72}, {"text": "means.", "start": 473.12, "duration": 4.079}, {"text": "We are deeply concerned by the", "start": 475.199, "duration": 4.161}, {"text": "persistence of armed conflicts in", "start": 477.199, "duration": 4.72}, {"text": "different regions of the world and their", "start": 479.36, "duration": 6.239}, {"text": "devastating consequences for civilians.", "start": 481.919, "duration": 6.56}, {"text": "In every case, our position rests on the", "start": 485.599, "duration": 5.44}, {"text": "same principles. Respect for the charter", "start": 488.479, "duration": 5.041}, {"text": "and international law, the protection of", "start": 491.039, "duration": 5.84}, {"text": "civilians, safe humanitarian access, and", "start": 493.52, "duration": 5.84}, {"text": "dialogue and diplomacy as indispensable", "start": 496.879, "duration": 4.88}, {"text": "paths towards a just, sustainable, and", "start": 499.36, "duration": 4.88}, {"text": "lasting peace.", "start": 501.759, "duration": 4.961}, {"text": "We must not grow accustomed to war. We", "start": 504.24, "duration": 5.04}, {"text": "must not accept violence as a permanent", "start": 506.72, "duration": 5.759}, {"text": "condition of our time or allow entire", "start": 509.28, "duration": 5.999}, {"text": "generations to grow up believing that", "start": 512.479, "duration": 4.961}, {"text": "force is the only way to resolve our", "start": 515.279, "duration": 6.56}, {"text": "differences. Guatemala stands for peace.", "start": 517.44, "duration": 6.959}, {"text": "This December, we will mark 30 years", "start": 521.839, "duration": 4.56}, {"text": "since the signing of the agreement on a", "start": 524.399, "duration": 4.641}, {"text": "firm and lasting peace, which brought an", "start": 526.399, "duration": 5.281}, {"text": "end to 36 years of internal armed", "start": 529.04, "duration": 6.239}, {"text": "conflict. After years of negotiation, we", "start": 531.68, "duration": 6.88}, {"text": "chose to replace armed violence with the", "start": 535.279, "duration": 6.0}, {"text": "pursuit of dialogue. That is why we", "start": 538.56, "duration": 4.719}, {"text": "understand the value of international", "start": 541.279, "duration": 4.481}, {"text": "support and the role of the United", "start": 543.279, "duration": 4.641}, {"text": "Nations.", "start": 545.76, "duration": 4.079}, {"text": "Our experience allows us to share one", "start": 547.92, "duration": 4.96}, {"text": "conviction. Negotiation is not a sign of", "start": 549.839, "duration": 5.361}, {"text": "weakness. Dialogue does not mean", "start": 552.88, "duration": 5.28}, {"text": "abandoning our principles. Seeking peace", "start": 555.2, "duration": 6.56}, {"text": "must never mean accepting injustice.", "start": 558.16, "duration": 5.52}, {"text": "We have also contributed to United", "start": 561.76, "duration": 4.56}, {"text": "Nations peacekeeping operations.", "start": 563.68, "duration": 6.159}, {"text": "More than 6,300 Guatemalan women and men", "start": 566.32, "duration": 5.68}, {"text": "have served under the United Nations", "start": 569.839, "duration": 5.521}, {"text": "flag in peacekeeping operations", "start": 572.0, "duration": 7.04}, {"text": "in different parts of the world.", "start": 575.36, "duration": 5.919}, {"text": "A country that knows the cost of war", "start": 579.04, "duration": 5.04}, {"text": "must also take responsibility for", "start": 581.279, "duration": 5.601}, {"text": "helping others preserve peace.", "start": 584.08, "duration": 4.64}, {"text": "Mr. President,", "start": 586.88, "duration": 3.68}, {"text": "we must strengthen the timely exchange", "start": 588.72, "duration": 5.04}, {"text": "of information, operational and judicial", "start": 590.56, "duration": 5.839}, {"text": "coordination, border security with", "start": 593.76, "duration": 5.28}, {"text": "respect for human rights, the protection", "start": 596.399, "duration": 5.761}, {"text": "of ports and transit routes, financial", "start": 599.04, "duration": 5.52}, {"text": "and asset investigations, and the", "start": 602.16, "duration": 4.32}, {"text": "recovery of assets derived from illicit", "start": 604.56, "duration": 4.56}, {"text": "activities. We must also work together", "start": 606.48, "duration": 5.12}, {"text": "on prevention.", "start": 609.12, "duration": 4.399}, {"text": "Lasting security cannot be achieved", "start": 611.6, "duration": 4.72}, {"text": "through law enforcement alone. It", "start": 613.519, "duration": 4.88}, {"text": "requires education, decent work,", "start": 616.32, "duration": 3.759}, {"text": "resilient communities, accessible", "start": 618.399, "duration": 4.0}, {"text": "institutions, and opportunities for", "start": 620.079, "duration": 5.121}, {"text": "young people. It requires us to reduce", "start": 622.399, "duration": 5.041}, {"text": "the social, territorial, and economic", "start": 625.2, "duration": 5.28}, {"text": "spaces that criminal structures exploit", "start": 627.44, "duration": 6.16}, {"text": "to recruit, exert control, and supplant", "start": 630.48, "duration": 6.4}, {"text": "the state. Our regional cooperation must", "start": 633.6, "duration": 5.359}, {"text": "be grounded in trust, shared", "start": 636.88, "duration": 4.079}, {"text": "responsibility, and respect for", "start": 638.959, "duration": 4.56}, {"text": "sovereignty. It must not serve private", "start": 640.959, "duration": 5.361}, {"text": "agendas or become an instrument of", "start": 643.519, "duration": 5.921}, {"text": "interests alien to our peoples. Climate", "start": 646.32, "duration": 5.36}, {"text": "change, pandemics, transnational", "start": 649.44, "duration": 5.519}, {"text": "organized crime, food insecurity,", "start": 651.68, "duration": 6.0}, {"text": "human mobility, and technological", "start": 654.959, "duration": 6.081}, {"text": "transformation all demand cooperation.", "start": 657.68, "duration": 6.399}, {"text": "Guatemala, a country particularly", "start": 661.04, "duration": 4.64}, {"text": "vulnerable to the effects of climate", "start": 664.079, "duration": 4.561}, {"text": "change, knows that adaptation, risk", "start": 665.68, "duration": 5.2}, {"text": "management, and the protection of rural", "start": 668.64, "duration": 5.439}, {"text": "livelihoods require national efforts,", "start": 670.88, "duration": 6.16}, {"text": "but also financing and cooperation", "start": 674.079, "duration": 5.681}, {"text": "commensurate with the needs capable of", "start": 677.04, "duration": 4.88}, {"text": "building capacity and delivering", "start": 679.76, "duration": 5.199}, {"text": "results. Defending multilateralism does", "start": 681.92, "duration": 5.52}, {"text": "not mean defending the status quo. The", "start": 684.959, "duration": 4.721}, {"text": "United Nations must become more", "start": 687.44, "duration": 4.639}, {"text": "effective, representative, transparent,", "start": 689.68, "duration": 5.12}, {"text": "and responsive to people.", "start": 692.079, "duration": 4.241}, {"text": "It must make better use of its", "start": 694.8, "duration": 4.08}, {"text": "resources, reduce duplication, and", "start": 696.32, "duration": 5.12}, {"text": "respond more swiftly without weakening", "start": 698.88, "duration": 5.6}, {"text": "the purposes for which it was created.", "start": 701.44, "duration": 5.76}, {"text": "Efficiency must strengthen, not erode,", "start": 704.48, "duration": 5.039}, {"text": "its three pillars: peace and security,", "start": 707.2, "duration": 4.0}, {"text": "sustainable development, and human", "start": 709.519, "duration": 4.88}, {"text": "rights. Effectiveness cannot be measured", "start": 711.2, "duration": 5.759}, {"text": "solely in administrative terms, but", "start": 714.399, "duration": 5.201}, {"text": "rather by the ability to prevent a war,", "start": 716.959, "duration": 4.88}, {"text": "protect a population under threat,", "start": 719.6, "duration": 4.96}, {"text": "combat hunger, confront transnational", "start": 721.839, "duration": 6.081}, {"text": "criminal networks, or support a state in", "start": 724.56, "duration": 7.279}, {"text": "strengthening its institutions.", "start": 727.92, "duration": 6.24}, {"text": "We do not need a United Nations that is", "start": 731.839, "duration": 4.481}, {"text": "smaller in purpose. We need a United", "start": 734.16, "duration": 5.04}, {"text": "Nations that is stronger in results and", "start": 736.32, "duration": 5.68}, {"text": "firmer in defending democratic", "start": 739.2, "duration": 5.92}, {"text": "principles. That transformation must", "start": 742.0, "duration": 6.079}, {"text": "also reach the Security Council. Its", "start": 745.12, "duration": 5.279}, {"text": "composition must better reflect the", "start": 748.079, "duration": 5.601}, {"text": "realities of the 21st century and remedy", "start": 750.399, "duration": 6.161}, {"text": "the long-standing under representation", "start": 753.68, "duration": 6.08}, {"text": "of entire regions. When the veto causes", "start": 756.56, "duration": 6.0}, {"text": "paralysis in the face of serious threats", "start": 759.76, "duration": 5.28}, {"text": "to international peace and security,", "start": 762.56, "duration": 6.56}, {"text": "confidence in the entire system suffers.", "start": 765.04, "duration": 7.2}, {"text": "We also face an important decision for", "start": 769.12, "duration": 5.68}, {"text": "the future of the organization.", "start": 772.24, "duration": 4.8}, {"text": "This election of the next secretary", "start": 774.8, "duration": 4.32}, {"text": "general.", "start": 777.04, "duration": 4.16}, {"text": "Guatemala hopes that the process will be", "start": 779.12, "duration": 4.959}, {"text": "transparent and inclusive and will", "start": 781.2, "duration": 5.52}, {"text": "identify an independent leader able to", "start": 784.079, "duration": 6.401}, {"text": "build bridges, defend the principles of", "start": 786.72, "duration": 6.48}, {"text": "the charter and lead the reform our", "start": 790.48, "duration": 5.84}, {"text": "organization needs. The Latin American", "start": 793.2, "duration": 5.52}, {"text": "and Caribbean region stands ready and", "start": 796.32, "duration": 4.48}, {"text": "prepared to shoulder its responsibility", "start": 798.72, "duration": 4.64}, {"text": "to the international community. The time", "start": 800.8, "duration": 5.12}, {"text": "has come for a Latin American woman to", "start": 803.36, "duration": 4.56}, {"text": "serve as Secretary General of the United", "start": 805.92, "duration": 4.08}, {"text": "Nations.", "start": 807.92, "duration": 4.56}, {"text": "Excellencies, distinguished delegates,", "start": 810.0, "duration": 4.56}, {"text": "the Republic of Guatemala reaffirms its", "start": 812.48, "duration": 3.84}, {"text": "commitment to the peaceful settlement of", "start": 814.56, "duration": 4.32}, {"text": "disputes and the observance of", "start": 816.32, "duration": 5.68}, {"text": "international law. We welcome the fact", "start": 818.88, "duration": 5.44}, {"text": "that the International Court of Justice", "start": 822.0, "duration": 6.959}, {"text": "has set the date for the oral hearings", "start": 824.32, "duration": 7.519}, {"text": "concerning the territorial, insular, and", "start": 828.959, "duration": 5.841}, {"text": "maritime dispute with bellies.", "start": 831.839, "duration": 4.641}, {"text": "For my country, this is more than a", "start": 834.8, "duration": 3.68}, {"text": "procedural milestone with the", "start": 836.48, "duration": 5.2}, {"text": "notification of the hearings. The final", "start": 838.48, "duration": 5.52}, {"text": "procedural stage before the court", "start": 841.68, "duration": 4.719}, {"text": "delivers its judgment has begun. It", "start": 844.0, "duration": 5.12}, {"text": "marks the culmination of a legal dispute", "start": 846.399, "duration": 4.8}, {"text": "that has accompanied the people of", "start": 849.12, "duration": 4.399}, {"text": "Guatemala and successive governments", "start": 851.199, "duration": 5.76}, {"text": "since independence and whose conclusion", "start": 853.519, "duration": 5.841}, {"text": "we eagerly await.", "start": 856.959, "duration": 4.481}, {"text": "We recognize that the court's judgment", "start": 859.36, "duration": 4.8}, {"text": "once delivered will bring the dispute to", "start": 861.44, "duration": 5.44}, {"text": "an end and we trust that it will provide", "start": 864.16, "duration": 5.44}, {"text": "legal certainty to both parties and lay", "start": 866.88, "duration": 4.8}, {"text": "the foundations for a new chapter in", "start": 869.6, "duration": 5.679}, {"text": "relations between Guatemala and BISE. In", "start": 871.68, "duration": 5.92}, {"text": "closing, I wish to say that Guatemala", "start": 875.279, "duration": 4.481}, {"text": "will continue to do its part,", "start": 877.6, "duration": 4.239}, {"text": "strengthening democratic institutions", "start": 879.76, "duration": 3.84}, {"text": "capable of meeting the needs of our", "start": 881.839, "duration": 4.401}, {"text": "people, resolutely confronting", "start": 883.6, "duration": 5.359}, {"text": "transnational organized crime and those", "start": 886.24, "duration": 5.68}, {"text": "who seek to capture institutions,", "start": 888.959, "duration": 4.641}, {"text": "defending international law", "start": 891.92, "duration": 3.2}, {"text": "consistently,", "start": 893.6, "duration": 4.64}, {"text": "promoting regional responses based on", "start": 895.12, "duration": 5.12}, {"text": "shared responsibility,", "start": 898.24, "duration": 5.2}, {"text": "and working for a United Nations capable", "start": 900.24, "duration": 5.039}, {"text": "of transforming itself. health to", "start": 903.44, "duration": 3.92}, {"text": "fulfill the promise contained in the", "start": 905.279, "duration": 4.401}, {"text": "opening words of our charter. We the", "start": 907.36, "duration": 7.279}, {"text": "peoples. Restoring trust will depend on", "start": 909.68, "duration": 7.92}, {"text": "our ability to show that even in times", "start": 914.639, "duration": 5.521}, {"text": "of uncertainty and division, we remain", "start": 917.6, "duration": 5.599}, {"text": "capable of building together solutions", "start": 920.16, "duration": 6.16}, {"text": "that none of us could achieve alone.", "start": 923.199, "duration": 6.681}, {"text": "Thank you very much.", "start": 926.32, "duration": 3.56}, {"text": "I thank the Minister of Foreign Affairs", "start": 934.079, "duration": 5.721}, {"text": "of Guatemala.", "start": 936.32, "duration": 3.48}]